    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d474">

                <pb facs="0683" n="595" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg595"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Newberry to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-09-26"><hi rendition="#italic">September 26,
                        1892</hi></date>. (Received October 13.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 547.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to herewith inclose for
                    your information copy of a letter from Dr. Bowen, of the Bible House, regarding
                    the seizure of a lot of Bibles at the town of Geybize. Also copy of my note to
                    the minister of foreign affairs on the same subject.</p>
                <p>I also called on the grand vizier, and read to him a memorandum of the case. He
                    immediately dictated a telegram to the authorities of Geybize ordering the
                    return of the books and future nonmolestation.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. R. Newberry</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires ad interim.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d474-a1.xml" xpointer="d474-a1"/>
